 "path": "memory/continual-arc-task-bb67ff0d.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC task-bb67ff0d\n\nObserved rule from demo pair 1 and confirmed correct test submission: shift the entire grid down by one row, filling the first row with the background color and dropping the original last row. In other words, for output row 0 use all background; for each row r>=1, copy input row r-1. Demo background was 6 and test background was 7, so use the grid's own background color (the dominant color), not a hard-coded value. Test case had 4x7 input and the correct output was rows `[7,7,7,7,7,7,7]`, `[7,7,0,7,7,7,7]`, `[7,0,7,7,7,7,7]`, `[7,7,0,7,7,7,7]`. Demo confirms the one-row downward translation of all cells, with the last row cropped.\n"
}
